Prefer the threading oslo.service backend

oslo.messaging selects an oslo.service backend when first imported, and
with no hook registered that is eventlet, which keystone does not use.
Register a default hook, as glance does, so threading is chosen unless a
backend was selected explicitly.

This saves nothing alone: futurist ("Do not import eventlet until it is
needed."), oslo.utils eventletutils and oslo_messaging/_utils.py also
import eventlet. With those fixed, anonymous RSS in the probe falls from
95MB to 73MB (81MB with the previous change alone).

Prompt: Mikal asked for privsep memory fixes that can be landed one at a
time and measured in devstack CI; keystone is one of the larger services.

